== Cultivation ==
A few species of kurrajong are popular garden trees and have been introduced to hot dry regions including the [[Mediterranean basin|Mediterranean]], [[South Africa]] and the western [[United States]]. These species are also hybridised for horticultural purposes, ''B. populneo-acerifolius'' being one example. Kurrajongs are known to bloom erratically in cultivation.

